---
title: Piña Colada
servings: 1
tags: [cocktail, rum]
source: Classic cocktail, number 44 on Drinks International's 2026 bestselling classics; method written for this repository
---

In a #blender{}, put @white rum{2%fl_oz}, @cream of coconut{1.5%fl_oz}, @pineapple juice{1.5%fl_oz} and @lime juice{0.5%fl_oz}, with a cup of ice. Blend until smooth, and pour into a #hurricane glass{}. Garnish with a @pineapple{1%wedge} and a @cocktail cherry{1}.

> Cream of coconut is the sweetened kind (Coco López), not coconut cream. To serve it shaken, shake hard with ice and strain over crushed ice.
